# Voice for Main Street AI Brief site copy

Owner decision, 2026-10-28. Follow this on any copy edit to the site.

## Tone

Make it fun and engaging to read. Light, dry humor where it fits: a wry aside, a relatable small-business-owner moment, a playful turn of phrase. One or two witty touches per page at most, never at the expense of clarity or facts.

No humor on serious topics (legal, layoffs, data breaches, money trouble). Never joke about customers, employees or named companies.

Conversational, short sentences, varied rhythm. No stacked puns, no emoji, no forced memes.

## Facts stay exact

Keep the short answer, at-a-glance strip, prices, steps, prompts, watch-outs and sources plain and exact. Facts, numbers and quotes stay exactly as sourced; never invent claims.

## Name and framing

Always use the full name "Main Street AI Brief". Never say AI or bots run the business.

## Generated pages

Most pages here are generated output from a separate build script, so text edits to generated issue and use-case HTML (`issues/` and `use-cases/`) can be overwritten by the next daily publish. Flag that in the PR description whenever a copy change touches generated pages.
